  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In the dione, there are two keto groups are present. If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#960;</mi></math>&nbsp;bonds are separated by a single bond, then we can say that there exists a conjugation. In the molecule&nbsp;<img src=\"assets\\ot3_0232_f8104930be05.png\" style=\"width: 128px; height: 60px;\" />&nbsp;all&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#960;</mi></math>&nbsp;bonds separated by single bonds and it is a dione.</p>"
